course: dictionary
lesson: 8393
title: Rude and polite words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rude means not polite. It describes words or actions that are unkind or show no respect for other people. Context helps you spot it: «Calling someone stupid is rude» tells you that name-calling is rude, even though the sentence does not say so directly.
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning. «A rude awakening» does not mean someone was impolite. It means a sudden, unpleasant surprise. Look at the words around rude to find out which meaning the writer chose.
explain: Rules about rudeness can change from place to place. «New places have new words, and they can sound rude when they're friendly.» So when a word sounds rude to you, ask whether it really is rude, or whether it is just new to you.
fact: Rude means not polite, or unkind and showing no respect.
fact: Interrupting, staring, pushing in and ignoring someone who speaks to you are all rude.
fact: «A rude awakening» means a sudden, unpleasant surprise.
fact: For hundreds of years people avoided saying the names of God, the Devil and hell out loud, because it felt rude or unlucky.
fact: «C'est nul» means "It's rubbish"; nul is not a rude word.
exercise: «Calling someone stupid is rude, so English has dozens of jokey ways to say it.» What does rude mean in this sentence? | Quick and clever | *Not polite and unkind | Funny and silly | Very loud and noisy
exercise: In the King's line «Don't be impertinent», impertinent means cheeky, which is close to rude. What does impertinent mean? | *Cheeky | Sleepy | Kind and gentle | Quiet and shy
exercise: «C'est nul» means "It's rubbish". Is nul a rude word? | *No, it means rubbish and is not rude | Yes, it means happy | Yes, it is French for rude | Yes, it is a very rude word
test: Which of these is rude? | Saying please | Waiting for your turn | Holding the door open | *Pushing in front of others in a queue
test: «A rude awakening» means what? | A polite way to say good morning | A loud alarm clock that rings nicely | *A sudden, unpleasant surprise | A happy morning in bed
exam: Ella says «it's rude to stare» at people. What does this tell us about staring? | It means looking at the sky | It is a good way to make friends | It is a kind way to say hello | *It is not polite to stare at people
